NOTICE OF THE RIGHT TO CONVERT GROUP LIFE INSURANCE TO AN INDIVIDUAL POLICY

Date: {{noticeDate}}

To: {{employeeName}}

From: {{companyName}}, on behalf of the plan administrator of {{planName}}

Re: Your Right to Convert Group Life Insurance Coverage Under California Insurance Code Section 10209

This notice concerns a right that is separate from, and unaffected by, any continuation-of-coverage notice you may separately receive regarding group HEALTH insurance (for example, under the federal COBRA statute or California's Cal-COBRA statute). Those laws govern continuation of group health-plan coverage. This notice instead concerns group LIFE insurance coverage under {{planName}} (policy number {{policyNumber}}, issued by {{insurerName}}), and the separate body of law that governs it: the California Insurance Code's provisions on group life policies.

1. Reason Coverage Under the Group Policy Is Ending. Your group life insurance coverage under {{planName}} is ending because your employment with {{companyName}} ended, effective {{separationDate}}.

2. Amount of Group Coverage in Force. The amount of your life insurance protection under the group policy at the time of termination was {{groupCoverageFaceAmount}}.

3. What This Notice Covers. The clauses that follow state what California Insurance Code Section 10209 provides about converting this group coverage to an individual policy, including the application deadline, the amount and type of policy available, what happens if death occurs during the conversion period, and the notice-timing rule that can extend the deadline. This notice summarizes that statute; it does not modify the actual terms of {{planName}} or of any individual policy that may be issued.

RECORD OF GROUP LIFE INSURANCE CONVERSION APPLICATION

I, {{employeeName}}, acknowledge that I received this notice regarding the right to convert group life insurance coverage under {{planName}} (policy number {{policyNumber}}, issued by {{insurerName}}) to an individual policy under California Insurance Code Section 10209.

My employment with {{companyName}} ended on {{separationDate}}. The amount of my life insurance protection under the group policy at that time was {{groupCoverageFaceAmount}}.

I understand that:
- Any application for an individual policy, together with the applicable first premium, must reach {{insurerName}} within 31 days after {{separationDate}} -- that is, by {{conversionApplicationDeadline}} -- unless the notice-timing extension described in this document applies.
- The individual policy, if issued under this statute, would be in a form other than term insurance and in an amount equal to my group coverage amount stated above.
- This record is not itself an application for coverage; any application must be submitted directly to {{insurerName}} using its own required forms.

